    "title": "AKI likely from gastroenteritis, not TDF",
    "message": "Guidelines note that in patients on TDF admitted to hospital, intercurrent illnesses with dehydration or sepsis may cause renal deterioration, requiring creatinine checking. The patient has severe gastroenteritis with 5 days of vomiting and diarrhoea, causing dehydration and AKI (creatinine 2.4, up from 0.9). A urea-to-creatinine ratio of 24:1 strongly supports a pre-renal cause from volume depletion rather than intrinsic TDF nephrotoxicity. Two household contacts share the same illness, reinforcing an infectious aetiology. Urinalysis shows no protein or glucose, which argues against TDF-induced proximal tubular damage. The clinician is considering stopping TDF permanently, but the evidence favours dehydration-related AKI that should resolve with fluid resuscitation. Permanent discontinuation may be unnecessary.",
